※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4566

※ A reference to an element of a list lends the whole list for as long as the
※ reference is kept, whichever element it names: joining onto the list may
※ move every element into new room and give the old room back, which would
※ leave `r` naming room nobody holds.  So the join is refused while `r` is
※ still used below it, as it is while a view of the list is out.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let l: mut [u8] = [1u8, 2u8] in ⎕heap
    let r: &mut u8 = &mut l⟦0⟧
    l ⧺← [3u8]
    r⌖ ← 5u8
    0u6
